        "code": {
          "text": "Suicidal ideation and risk assessment"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Passive suicidal ideation: 'easier if I didn't wake up.' Last week thought of overdosing on partner's sleeping tablets. No current active plan or intent today, but reports ambivalence: 'don't really care what happens to me half the time.' Formal suicidality screen assessed moderate risk. No previous suicide attempts; history of superficial cutting as a teenager. Patient agreed to seek help if suicidal ideation increases and was able to safety plan."
      }
